// PIN FMT-005 — a key written in quotes stays in quotes.
//
// A key reaches the AST as a bare `String` either way, so `#("k": 1)` and
// `#(k: 1)` are the same node — and the formatter, having to choose, printed
// every key that COULD be bare bare. `String("k")` became `Ident("k")`: a token
// change, however identical the value.
//
// Unfixable from the AST alone, so `NamedTupleExpr` records `quoted`, which is
// the remedy FORMATTER_RULES.md §12 names for exactly this. Both spellings are
// here, side by side, because the pin has to hold BOTH directions: quoting the
// bare one is the same bug in reverse.
mixto = #("k": 1, k2: 2)

>> mixto["k"] ¶
>> mixto.k2 ¶
